{"title":"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 48","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_48\">Problem 48</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 48\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/9/009cf3eeb0ff3789cc057632947cadb200ab4663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with medians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/a/cca6bcc3627fad46692f1d0ce6c489009bcb1cf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE, BF, CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffb105232a8a0e6307866e5d52ccb9e6db45c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> parallel and equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/476a3e4b646185debc56794ef05b819017596416.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH and HE$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" /> are drawn; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> extended meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. \nWhich one of the following statements is not necessarily correct? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315d1b60dd14266c714cfbb0ffbc5bb8b60e5a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ AEHF\\text{ is a parallelogram}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ HE=HG\\\\ \\textbf{(C)}\\ BH=DC\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ FG=\\frac{3}{4}AB\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ FG\\text{ is a median of triangle }BFH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We evaluate each statement using properties of triangles and parallelograms:\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Statement (A):</b> Quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea094bf5afb6865df297267b4f880ae80aad0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEHF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> has opposite sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fffb105232a8a0e6307866e5d52ccb9e6db45c33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a65c05bd85d2609bea5db2b109ed5f556463511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE$\" width=\"27\" height=\"13\" /> that are given to be parallel and equal in length (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/1/cc1dda31ef23088e067425dae830311963af4721.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH \\parallel AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/0/3b03d57ea85c28b226347013bd31128c54e9b582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FH = AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />). By definition, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea094bf5afb6865df297267b4f880ae80aad0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEHF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram. Thus, <b>(A)</b> is correct.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Statement (C) and (D):</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/a/2ea094bf5afb6865df297267b4f880ae80aad0b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AEHF$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> is a parallelogram, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/3/98368eedc0b5fffc38621a9bdf1fe141bb44baad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF \\parallel EH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57edfe3ec4ca5fcb6e7db36a59cd16047d50ae83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = EH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/d/c1ddead683e523de3c36e400b6edf638239e9665.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = FC = EH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"138\" height=\"14\" />, which means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/9/3896419cf512c105900d4ea01a71d2a718aade29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FEHC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"61\" height=\"14\" /> is also a parallelogram. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/edaaa4338e44930db7485ecabafb0e3dfa61776c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE = CH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"86\" height=\"14\" />.</li></ul>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> is a midline of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/22865a26346e73d6c2dfc0a94b72475e5755c17b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE \\parallel AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/a/25afde33af06ad9b79c8922f068b1c1948299cab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE = \\frac{1}{2}AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/7/ce7cb063ae41e0bc7961b843186f600be909ac87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BHC$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/b/52b3b006e6f9fe1681bd1f340795f789d888318e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FE$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> extended passes through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />) and is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />. By the converse of the Midpoint Theorem, this line intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> at its midpoint <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/6/1c670fef2b129de960309bf9874dcd5d9fad8d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EG = \\frac{1}{2}CH = \\frac{1}{2}FE = \\frac{1}{4}AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"230\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/e/d5e97bfaf09c8a5436802c6d72d5b35f062a340a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG = FE + EG = \\frac{1}{2}AB + \\frac{1}{4}AB = \\frac{3}{4}AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"329\" height=\"38\" />, so <b>(D)</b> is correct.\n</p>\n<ul><li><b>Statement (E):</b> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951902c11a1cd39a091ea15f0f06cbc79095de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> connects vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to the midpoint of the opposite side in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/99310ff5d780f4de4fb18f01c5dd812b1d51177b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951902c11a1cd39a091ea15f0f06cbc79095de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is a median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/3/99310ff5d780f4de4fb18f01c5dd812b1d51177b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BFH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, making <b>(E)</b> correct.</li></ul>\n<ul><li><b>Statement (B):</b> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de5e54474424563d063e10867992179472f410e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HE = AF = \\frac{1}{2}AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"150\" height=\"38\" />, whereas <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/6/e7659b3cf9e6d214b6798fd4d079c9f215dddf3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG = \\frac{1}{2}BH$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"101\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" /> are not equal in a general triangle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/a/c2a7aa5b7bd10c798cf32c06d697b5aa692b68e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HE = HG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"88\" height=\"14\" /> is not necessarily correct.</li></ul>\n<p>Thus, the statement that is not necessarily correct is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b7193f66028e13f331d53ff5e6942c4b05587465.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_48&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME\" title=\"1955 AHSME\">1955 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1955 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1955\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_49\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 49\">Problem 49</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_50\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 50\">Problem 50</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"1955 AHSME Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1955_AHSME_Problems/Problem_20\" title